# Alize — Cursor rules (mirror of AGENTS.md; read AGENTS.md for full detail)

## Status: PLANNING. Do not implement product features until the Decisions Log in AGENTS.md is filled. If ambiguous → ask the human.

## Hard constraints
- **C1 Frontend-only on Vercel.** No long-running servers.
- **C2 BYOK.** Use the human's own AI API key; never bake in paid inference.
- **C3 Local-first.** Projects/chats/keys live in the browser (IndexedDB/Dexie). No managed-backend dependency to function. Cloud sync is optional & later.
- **C4 AI prompt → working app** is the core UX.
- **C5 Web / PWA.**
- **C6 Architecture + scaffold first.**

## Provisional stack (pending Q&A)
Next.js 15 · React 19 · TypeScript strict · Tailwind · shadcn/ui · Zustand · Vercel AI SDK · Dexie · pnpm + Turborepo · Biome · Vitest · Playwright.

## Agent rules
1. Memory first: `graphify query "<q>"` before grep; `graphify update .` after edits.
2. Don't assume — check AGENTS.md Decisions Log; ask when unsure.
3. Strict TS, no `any` without a comment.
4. Prefer `context7` MCP for current docs (Next.js/React/Tailwind/AI SDK/shadcn) over guessing.
5. Commits only on `arena/019f976c-alize`.
6. Quality gates before done: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test`.

See `AGENTS.md` (Decisions Log, command map) and `docs/agent-tooling.md` (MCP setup).
